plugin-qualify (0.20.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: 0.20.6, the qualification domain in plugin-qualify-contract
  * records package: depend on plugin-qualify by a floor only
  * test: the records package depends on plugin-qualify by a floor only (red)
  * packaging: floors only, no version ceiling on a dependency
  * packaging: prune the bundled dependency trees to what the packages publish
  * test: the bundled dependency trees carry no dotfile, spec or test
    directory (red)
  * ci: the tests that need omx-contract installed run in a Fedora container
    job
  * test: the installed package carries every module the built program imports
  * release: the install job proves the installed program loads its run-time
    modules and domain
  * ci: the unit jobs install omx-contract 3.20.0 from the channel
  * packaging: ship ajv in the installed package, beside the code that
    imports it
  * release: install plugin-qualify-contract with the package, rpm and deb
  * packaging: the contract package synopsis starts without an article
  * test: stanza returns the found paragraph without an index read
  * packaging: omx-contract floor 3.20.0, where the installer's domain mode is
  * test: the installer call spans its continuation line
  * qualification.json: the one formatting of omx-contract fmt
  * packaging: plugin-qualify requires plugin-qualify-contract of the same
    version
  * packaging: the qualification domain ships in the plugin-qualify-contract
    subpackage
  * packaging: install the qualification domain with the installer's domain
    mode
  * test: the spec and debian/rules call the installer's domain mode
    directly; fmt check uses the installed command (red)
  * test: the qualification domain ships in plugin-qualify-contract,
    installed by the installer's domain mode (red)
  * qualification domain: OMX_CONTRACT_PATH is a colon list whose first
    directory holding the domain wins, and $id must be the domain's
  * qualification domain: info.x-stability is required (experimental or
    stable) and the document states experimental
  * qualification domain: the TODO beside the schema const names
    omx-contract#113
  * qualification domain: a page hands the document with init(doc), the CLIs
    read OMX_CONTRACT_PATH, the library reads the installed path only
  * qualification domain: the C codes header is removed, no item is marked
    for one
  * qualification domain: items named QUALIFICATION_*, $schema stated, no
    render, words read from the installed JSON
  * schema addresses: the descriptor writers and their field fixtures name
    https://openmixer.org/schema/omx-contract/v3/, not a code-hosting address
  * qualification domain: memory-bound is a declared word the measurer reads
    rendered, and the rpm and deb install the domain (omx-contract#81)
  * qualification domain: contract.d/qualification and its TypeScript render,
    moved from omx-contract (omx-contract#81 move 2)
  * The sync fills plugin-db's store, in plugin-db's grammar (#73)

